3.3 The Chairperson shall preside at all meetings of the Committee and shall be responsible for maintaining order and ensuring that business is conducted in accordance with these Standing Orders. The Chairperson shall have a deliberative vote only. [Amended 13 March 2025: inserted the words “and shall be responsible for maintaining order” after “Committee”.]

3.4 The Deputy Chairperson shall perform the duties of the Chairperson in the Chairperson’s absence.

3.5 The Secretary shall:
(a) issue notices of meetings;
(b) prepare and circulate agendas and minutes;
(c) maintain the register of members;
(d) conduct the correspondence of the Committee.

3.6 The Treasurer shall:
(a) maintain the financial records of the Committee;
(b) present a financial statement at each general meeting;
(c) prepare the annual budget for approval by the Committee;
(d) report to the Committee on any expenditure exceeding the approved budget.

3.7 In the event of a casual vacancy in any office, the Committee shall elect a replacement at the next general meeting.

---

PART 4 – MEETINGS

4.1 The Committee shall meet at least six (6) times per year. Meetings shall be held on the second Tuesday of the month at 6:00 pm, unless the Committee resolves otherwise. [Amended 2 May 2024: replaced “monthly” with “at least six (6) times per year”.]

4.2 Meetings shall be held at Marrickville Library, or at such other venue as the Committee may from time to time determine. [Amended 2 May 2024: added reference to alternate venues.]

4.3 The Chairperson may call a special meeting at any time, and shall do so upon the written request of at least three (3) members.

4.4 Notice of each meeting shall be given to members at least seven (7) clear days prior to the meeting, and shall include the agenda and any supporting papers.

4.5 No business shall be transacted at any meeting unless a quorum is present. The constitution states that the Marrickville Community Library Programming Committee meeting_quorum shall be 5 members. Record status: current. This quorum requirement is current and shall apply to all general meetings of the Committee.

4.6 If a quorum is not present within thirty (30) minutes of the advertised commencement time, the meeting shall stand adjourned to the same time and place in the following week. If a quorum is not present at the adjourned meeting, the members present shall constitute the quorum for that meeting, provided that no fewer than three (3) members are present.

4.7 Questions arising at any meeting shall be decided by a majority of votes of members present and voting. The Chairperson shall have a deliberative vote only, except in the case of an equality of votes, in which case the Chairperson shall have a casting vote.

---

PART 5 – AGENDAS AND MINUTES

5.1 The Secretary shall prepare the agenda for each meeting in consultation with the Chairperson. Items for inclusion may be submitted by any member to the Secretary no later than five (5) clear days prior to the meeting.

5.2 The agenda shall include:
(a) apologies;
(b) confirmation of previous minutes;
(c) business arising from previous minutes;
(d) reports from office bearers;
(e) program reports and upcoming events;
(f) general business;
(g) date of next meeting.

5.3 Minutes of each meeting shall be recorded by the Secretary and circulated to members within fourteen (14) days of the meeting. Minutes shall be confirmed at the next meeting and signed by the Chairperson.

5.4 The minutes shall record the names of members present, the business considered, and the resolutions passed. Motions and amendments shall be recorded in full. [Amended 2 May 2024: added requirement to record motions and amendments in full.]

---

PART 6 – VOTING AND DECISIONS

7.4 The Chairperson shall preside at all meetings of the Committee and of the Annual General Meeting. The Chairperson shall represent the Committee on public occasions and shall be a signatory on the Committee's bank accounts.

7.5 The Deputy Chairperson shall perform the duties of the Chairperson in the Chairperson's absence. In the absence of both the Chairperson and Deputy Chairperson, the meeting shall elect a Chairperson for that meeting from among the members present.

7.6 The Secretary shall:
(a) give notice of all meetings and prepare agendas in accordance with Part 5;
(b) record and circulate minutes within fourteen (14) days of each meeting;
(c) maintain the register of correspondence;
(d) have custody of the Committee's records and documents, other than financial records held by the Treasurer;
(e) conduct the general correspondence of the Committee.

7.7 The Programs Officer shall:
(a) coordinate the development of the annual program of events and activities;
(b) liaise with library staff regarding room bookings, equipment, and permits;
(c) prepare program reports for each meeting;
(d) oversee the evaluation of programs and events.

7.8 The Membership Officer shall:
(a) maintain the register of members and their contact details;
(b) process applications for membership in accordance with Part 3;
(c) issue membership cards and receipts for subscriptions;
(d) report on membership numbers and trends at each meeting.

7.9 The Publicity Officer shall:
(a) prepare and distribute publicity material for programs and events;
(b) maintain the Committee's social media accounts and website content;
(c) liaise with local media and community organisations;
(d) report on publicity outcomes at each meeting.

7.10 Treasurer – Duties and Reporting

7.10.1 The Treasurer shall have custody of all funds of the Committee and shall bank them promptly in the name of the Committee in an account approved by the Committee.

7.10.2 The Treasurer shall keep proper books of account showing all receipts and expenditure, and shall preserve all vouchers and receipts for a period of at least seven (7) years.

7.10.3 The Treasurer shall prepare a financial report for each ordinary meeting of the Committee, showing:
(a) the balance of each account at the date of the report;
(b) all receipts and payments since the last report;
(c) any outstanding commitments or liabilities;
(d) any matters requiring the attention of the Committee.

7.10.4 Standing orders require Priya Sharma treasurer_report_due_day to be the third Thursday. Record status: current. This requirement is current and applies to all financial reports presented at ordinary meetings of the Committee. The Treasurer shall ensure that the financial report is tabled at each ordinary meeting, which shall be held on the third Thursday of each month, unless the Committee resolves otherwise for a particular month.

7.10.5 In addition to the report at ordinary meetings, the Treasurer shall present a full financial statement at the Annual General Meeting, covering the financial year ending 30 June. The statement shall include:
(a) an income and expenditure statement;
(b) a statement of assets and liabilities;
(c) a report on any grants received or applied for during the year.

7.10.6 The Treasurer shall prepare an annual budget for the forthcoming financial year and present it to the Committee for adoption no later than the ordinary meeting held in May.

7.10.7 The Treasurer shall be a signatory on the Committee's bank accounts. All cheques and electronic payments shall be signed or authorised by any two (2) of the following: Chairperson, Secretary, Treasurer. [Amended 14 March 2024: added requirement for two signatories on all payments.]

